//! The `timeline-trigger-activation-range` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS)
//! [shorthand
//! property](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Shorthand_properties)
//! specifies the start and end of a [scroll-triggered
//! animation](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Animation_triggers/Using_scroll-triggered_animations)
//! trigger's activation range.
//!
//! Initial: timeline-trigger-activation-range-start: normal; timeline-trigger-activation-range-end:
//! normal. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: timeline-trigger-activation-range-start: Relative to the specified named timeline
//! range if specified, otherwise relative to the entire timeline;
//! timeline-trigger-activation-range-end: Relative to the specified named timeline range if
//! specified, otherwise relative to the entire timeline.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - normal: A `<length>` or `<percentage>` value specifies an offset from the beginning of the
//! `normal` timeline, which again defaults to
//! [`cover`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/timeline-range-name#cover)
//! for a `view()` progress timeline source, and
//! [`scroll`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/timeline-range-name#scroll)
//! for a `scroll()` progress timeline source. Negative values outset the start and end, resulting in
//! a longer activation range. Positive values inset the start and end of the activation range,
//! shortening it.
//!
//! Grammar: [ <'timeline-trigger-activation-range-start'> <'timeline-trigger-activation-range-end'>?
//! ]#
//!
//! Specification:
//! https://drafts.csswg.org/animation-triggers-1/#propdef-timeline-trigger-activation-range
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/timeline-trigger-activation-range
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

